Title: 0002-voteproblems-off-by-one
Repository: micropoliscore
Base-Commit: 69ccf87ed72d2d2950b70cf16ef1391439bd9d48
Requires: 0001-init-uninitialized-members.patch
Author: aros-micropolis project
Date: 2026-09-15
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: generic - any platform; benign-looking on WASM, crash source on native

Problem:
  voteProblems() resets its round-robin index with 'problem > PROBNUM', so the loop visits index PROBNUM before wrapping: it reads problemTable[PROBNUM] (past the 10-entry stack buffer in cityEvaluation) and increments problemVotes[PROBNUM] (past the member array, corrupting the following member). Caught by AddressSanitizer on the host at evaluate.cpp:298 during a 192-phase headless run of haight.cty.
Solution:
  Use '>= PROBNUM' so the index wraps at the array bound. One-character-class fix; behavior is unchanged for all valid indices.
Validation:
  Host: ASan build (build/host/harness), 192 phases of haight.cty, clean
  (2026-09-15). Guest: AROS One 1.3 (ABIv11) under QEMU/TCG, GCC 10.5.0,
  192 phases, clean exit, RESULT cityTime=4851 year=2001 month=0.
  Scope: headless
  harness only - no UI, no scenario path, no save.
Removal:
  Fill in when this is a workaround; permanent fixes say so here.

diff --git a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/evaluate.cpp b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/evaluate.cpp
index 6d41d5e..aad5b74 100644
--- a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/evaluate.cpp
+++ b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/evaluate.cpp
@@ -300,7 +300,11 @@ void Micropolis::voteProblems(const short problemTable[PROBNUM])
             voteCount++;
         }
         problem++;
-        if (problem > PROBNUM) {
+        // >=, not >: with '>' the loop visits index PROBNUM first, reading
+        // problemTable[PROBNUM] (stack OOB, caught by ASan on the host)
+        // and incrementing problemVotes[PROBNUM] (member OOB, silently
+        // corrupting whatever follows the array).
+        if (problem >= PROBNUM) {
             problem = 0;
         }
         loopCount++;
